  "behavior": [
    "Consistent Manage menus and accessible rename/removal dialogs with named consequences, Cancel focus and retained drafts on conflict.",
    "Account status/health/search filters, issues-first sorting, issue summaries, explicit reasons and unknown health.",
    "Separate registration search/status filters, removed history and restoration for unfinished registrations only.",
    "Central account rename synchronizes linked registration; removal revokes account access and invalidates registration review/tickets.",
    "Removal commits before desktop cleanup; cleanup failures have an explicit recovery action. Old desktop controls and new display connections reject removed registrations.",
    "Expected revisions, immutable operation identity and scoped actor/destination constraints protect concurrent edits and explicit retries."
  ],
  "corrections": [
    "The first isolated SQL fixture exposed an enum-literal assumption; health mapping now compares text values and the full fixture passed.",
